{"id":"G0049","name":"OilRig","aliases":["COBALT GYPSY","IRN2","APT34","Helix Kitten","Evasive Serpens","Hazel Sandstorm","EUROPIUM","ITG13","Earth Simnavaz","Crambus","TA452"],"url":"https://attack.mitre.org/groups/G0049","summary":"OilRig is a suspected Iranian threat group that has targeted Middle Eastern and international victims since at least 2014. The group has targeted a variety of sectors, including financial, government, energy, chemical, and telecommunications. It appears the group carries out supply chain attacks, leveraging the trust relationship between organizations to attack their primary targets. The group works on behalf of the Iranian government based on infrastructure details that contain references to Iran, use of Iranian infrastructure, and targeting that aligns with nation-state interests.","summaryCites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig April 2017","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/04/unit42-oilrig-actors-provide-glimpse-development-testing-efforts/"},{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}],"procedures":[{"id":"T1027.005","text":"OilRig has tested malware samples to determine AV detection and subsequently modified the samples to ensure AV evasion.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig April 2017","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/04/unit42-oilrig-actors-provide-glimpse-development-testing-efforts/"},{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Nov 2018","url":"https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/unit42-analyzing-oilrigs-ops-tempo-testing-weaponization-delivery/"}]},{"id":"T1027.013","text":"OilRig has encrypted and encoded data in its malware, including by using base64.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"Unit 42 QUADAGENT July 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-oilrig-targets-technology-service-provider-government-agency-quadagent/"},{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"}]},{"id":"T1036","text":"OilRig has used.doc file extensions to mask malicious executables.","cites":[{"name":"Check Point APT34 April 2021","url":"https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/irans-apt34-returns-with-an-updated-arsenal/"}]},{"id":"T1036.005","text":"OilRig has named a downloaded copy of the Plink tunneling utility as \\ProgramData\\Adobe.exe.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1070.004","text":"OilRig has deleted files associated with their payload after execution.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"}]},{"id":"T1078","text":"OilRig has used compromised credentials to access other systems on a victim network.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"Crowdstrike GTR2020 Mar 2020","url":"https://go.crowdstrike.com/rs/281-OBQ-266/images/Report2020CrowdStrikeGlobalThreatReport.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1078.002","text":"OilRig has used an exfiltration tool named STEALHOOK to retreive valid domain credentials.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1112","text":"OilRig has used reg.exe to modify system configuration.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"},{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1140","text":"A OilRig macro has run a PowerShell command to decode file contents. OilRig has also used certutil to decode base64-encoded files on victims.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"OilRig New Delivery Oct 2017","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/10/unit42-oilrig-group-steps-attacks-new-delivery-documents-new-injector-trojan/"},{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"}]},{"id":"T1218.001","text":"OilRig has used a CHM payload to load and execute another malicious file once delivered to a victim.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1497.001","text":"OilRig has used macros to verify if a mouse is connected to a compromised machine.","cites":[{"name":"Check Point APT34 April 2021","url":"https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/irans-apt34-returns-with-an-updated-arsenal/"}]},{"id":"T1553.002","text":"OilRig has signed its malware with stolen certificates.","cites":[{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}]},{"id":"T1556.002","text":"OilRig has registered a password filter DLL in order to drop malware.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1686.003","text":"OilRig has modified Windows firewall rules to enable remote access.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1583.001","text":"OilRig has set up fake VPN portals, conference sign ups, and job application websites to target victims.","cites":[{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}]},{"id":"T1586.002","text":"OilRig has compromised email accounts to send phishing emails.","cites":[{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}]},{"id":"T1587.001","text":"OilRig actively developed and used a series of downloaders during 2022.","cites":[{"name":"ESET OilRig Downloaders DEC 2023","url":"https://www.welivesecurity.com/en/eset-research/oilrig-persistent-attacks-cloud-service-powered-downloaders/"}]},{"id":"T1588.002","text":"OilRig has made use of the publicly available tools including Plink and Mimikatz.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"},{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1588.003","text":"OilRig has obtained stolen code signing certificates to digitally sign malware.","cites":[{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}]},{"id":"T1608.001","text":"OilRig has hosted malware on fake websites designed to target specific audiences.","cites":[{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}]},{"id":"T0817","text":"OilRig has been seen utilizing watering hole attacks to collect credentials which could be used to gain access into ICS networks.","cites":[{"name":"Eduard Kovacs May 2018","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220120001230/https://www.cyberviser.com/2018/05/group-linked-to-shamoon-attacks-targeting-ics-networks-in-middle-east-and-uk/"}]},{"id":"T0865","text":"OilRig used spearphishing emails with malicious Microsoft Excel spreadsheet attachments.","cites":[{"name":"Robert Falcone, Bryan Lee May 2016","url":"https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1133","text":"OilRig uses remote services such as VPN, Citrix, or OWA to persist in an environment.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"}]},{"id":"T1195","text":"OilRig has leveraged compromised organizations to conduct supply chain attacks on government entities.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1566.001","text":"OilRig has sent spearphising emails with malicious attachments to potential victims using compromised and/or spoofed email accounts.","cites":[{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"},{"name":"Unit 42 QUADAGENT July 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-oilrig-targets-technology-service-provider-government-agency-quadagent/"},{"name":"Crowdstrike Helix Kitten Nov 2018","url":"https://www.crowdstrike.com/blog/meet-crowdstrikes-adversary-of-the-month-for-november-helix-kitten/"}]},{"id":"T1566.002","text":"OilRig has sent spearphising emails with malicious links to potential victims.","cites":[{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"},{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/"}]},{"id":"T1566.003","text":"OilRig has used LinkedIn to send spearphishing links.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T0853","text":"OilRig has embedded a macro within spearphishing attachments that has been made up of both a VBScript and a PowerShell script.","cites":[{"name":"Robert Falcone, Bryan Lee May 2016","url":"https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1047","text":"OilRig has used WMI for execution.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1053.005","text":"OilRig has created scheduled tasks that run a VBScript to execute a payload on victim machines.","cites":[{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"},{"name":"Unit 42 QUADAGENT July 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-oilrig-targets-technology-service-provider-government-agency-quadagent/"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T1059","text":"OilRig has used various types of scripting for execution.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"OilRig ISMAgent July 2017","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/07/unit42-oilrig-uses-ismdoor-variant-possibly-linked-greenbug-threat-group/"},{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"}]},{"id":"T1059.001","text":"OilRig has used PowerShell scripts for execution, including use of a macro to run a PowerShell command to decode file contents.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"OilRig New Delivery Oct 2017","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/10/unit42-oilrig-group-steps-attacks-new-delivery-documents-new-injector-trojan/"},{"name":"Crowdstrike Helix Kitten Nov 2018","url":"https://www.crowdstrike.com/blog/meet-crowdstrikes-adversary-of-the-month-for-november-helix-kitten/"}]},{"id":"T1059.003","text":"OilRig has used macros to deliver malware such as QUADAGENT and OopsIE. OilRig has used batch scripts.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"OilRig ISMAgent July 2017","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/07/unit42-oilrig-uses-ismdoor-variant-possibly-linked-greenbug-threat-group/"},{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"}]},{"id":"T1059.005","text":"OilRig has used VBScript macros for execution on compromised hosts.","cites":[{"name":"Check Point APT34 April 2021","url":"https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/irans-apt34-returns-with-an-updated-arsenal/"}]},{"id":"T1203","text":"OilRig has exploited CVE-2024-30088 to run arbitrary code in the context of `SYSTEM`.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1204.001","text":"OilRig has delivered malicious links to achieve execution on the target system.","cites":[{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"},{"name":"Unit 42 QUADAGENT July 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-oilrig-targets-technology-service-provider-government-agency-quadagent/"},{"name":"Crowdstrike Helix Kitten Nov 2018","url":"https://www.crowdstrike.com/blog/meet-crowdstrikes-adversary-of-the-month-for-november-helix-kitten/"}]},{"id":"T1204.002","text":"OilRig has delivered macro-enabled documents that required targets to click the \"enable content\" button to execute the payload on the system.","cites":[{"name":"Unit 42 OopsIE! Feb 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/02/unit42-oopsie-oilrig-uses-threedollars-deliver-new-trojan/"},{"name":"Unit 42 QUADAGENT July 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-oilrig-targets-technology-service-provider-government-agency-quadagent/"},{"name":"Crowdstrike Helix Kitten Nov 2018","url":"https://www.crowdstrike.com/blog/meet-crowdstrikes-adversary-of-the-month-for-november-helix-kitten/"}]},{"id":"T0859","text":"OilRig utilized stolen credentials to gain access to victim machines.","cites":[{"name":"Dragos","url":"https://dragos.com/resource/allanite/"}]},{"id":"T1137.004","text":"OilRig has abused the Outlook Home Page feature for persistence. OilRig has also used CVE-2017-11774 to roll back the initial patch designed to protect against Home Page abuse.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye Outlook Dec 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/12/breaking-the-rules-tough-outlook-for-home-page-attacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1505.003","text":"OilRig has used web shells, often to maintain access to a victim network.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"Crowdstrike GTR2020 Mar 2020","url":"https://go.crowdstrike.com/rs/281-OBQ-266/images/Report2020CrowdStrikeGlobalThreatReport.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1543.003","text":"OilRig has used a compromised Domain Controller to create a service on a remote host.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1068","text":"OilRig has exploited the Windows Kernel Elevation of Privilege vulnerability, CVE-2024-30088.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1003.001","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tools such as Mimikatz to steal credentials to accounts logged into the compromised system and to Outlook Web Access.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT35 2018","url":"https://static.carahsoft.com/concrete/files/1015/2779/3571/M-Trends-2018-Report.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1003.004","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tools such as LaZagne to steal credentials to accounts logged into the compromised system and to Outlook Web Access.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT35 2018","url":"https://static.carahsoft.com/concrete/files/1015/2779/3571/M-Trends-2018-Report.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1003.005","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tools such as LaZagne to steal credentials to accounts logged into the compromised system and to Outlook Web Access.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT35 2018","url":"https://static.carahsoft.com/concrete/files/1015/2779/3571/M-Trends-2018-Report.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1056.001","text":"OilRig has employed keyloggers including KEYPUNCH and LONGWATCH.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"},{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1110","text":"OilRig has used brute force techniques to obtain credentials.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"IBM ZeroCleare Wiper December 2019","url":"https://securityintelligence.com/posts/new-destructive-wiper-zerocleare-targets-energy-sector-in-the-middle-east/"}]},{"id":"T1552.001","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tools such as LaZagne to steal credentials to accounts logged into the compromised system and to Outlook Web Access.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT35 2018","url":"https://static.carahsoft.com/concrete/files/1015/2779/3571/M-Trends-2018-Report.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1555","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tools such as LaZagne to steal credentials to accounts logged into the compromised system and to Outlook Web Access.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT35 2018","url":"https://static.carahsoft.com/concrete/files/1015/2779/3571/M-Trends-2018-Report.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1555.003","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tools such as LaZagne to steal credentials to accounts logged into the compromised system and to Outlook Web Access. OilRig has also used tool named PICKPOCKET to dump passwords from web browsers.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT35 2018","url":"https://static.carahsoft.com/concrete/files/1015/2779/3571/M-Trends-2018-Report.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1555.004","text":"OilRig has used credential dumping tool named VALUEVAULT to steal credentials from the Windows Credential Manager.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T1007","text":"OilRig has used `sc query` on a victim to gather information about services.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1012","text":"OilRig has used `reg query “HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Microsoft\\Terminal Server Client\\Default”` on a victim to query the Registry.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1016","text":"OilRig has run `ipconfig /all` on a victim.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig Oct 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/10/unit42-oilrig-malware-campaign-updates-toolset-and-expands-targets/"}]},{"id":"T1033","text":"OilRig has run `whoami` on a victim.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig Oct 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/10/unit42-oilrig-malware-campaign-updates-toolset-and-expands-targets/"},{"name":"Check Point APT34 April 2021","url":"https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/irans-apt34-returns-with-an-updated-arsenal/"}]},{"id":"T1046","text":"OilRig has used the publicly available tool SoftPerfect Network Scanner as well as a custom tool called GOLDIRONY to conduct network scanning.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"}]},{"id":"T1049","text":"OilRig has used `netstat -an` on a victim to get a listing of network connections.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1057","text":"OilRig has run `tasklist` on a victim's machine and used infostealers to capture processes.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"},{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1069.001","text":"OilRig has used `net localgroup administrators` to find local administrators on compromised systems.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"},{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1069.002","text":"OilRig has used `net group /domain`, `net group “domain admins” /domain`, and `net group “Exchange Trusted Subsystem” /domain` to find domain group permission settings.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1082","text":"OilRig has run `hostname` and `systeminfo` on a victim.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig Oct 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/10/unit42-oilrig-malware-campaign-updates-toolset-and-expands-targets/"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T1087.001","text":"OilRig has run `net user`, `net user /domain`, `net group “domain admins” /domain`, and `net group “Exchange Trusted Subsystem” /domain` to get account listings on a victim.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1087.002","text":"OilRig has run `net user`, `net user /domain`, `net group “domain admins” /domain`, and `net group “Exchange Trusted Subsystem” /domain` to get account listings on a victim.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1120","text":"OilRig has used tools to identify if a mouse is connected to a targeted system.","cites":[{"name":"Check Point APT34 April 2021","url":"https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/irans-apt34-returns-with-an-updated-arsenal/"}]},{"id":"T1201","text":"OilRig has used net.exe in a script with `net accounts /domain` to find the password policy of a domain.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye Targeted Attacks Middle East Banks","url":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200618235708/https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2016/05/targeted_attacksaga.html"}]},{"id":"T1021.001","text":"OilRig has used Remote Desktop Protocol for lateral movement. The group has also used tunneling tools to tunnel RDP into the environment.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"Crowdstrike GTR2020 Mar 2020","url":"https://go.crowdstrike.com/rs/281-OBQ-266/images/Report2020CrowdStrikeGlobalThreatReport.pdf"}]},{"id":"T1021.004","text":"OilRig has used Putty to access compromised systems.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"}]},{"id":"T1005","text":"OilRig has used PowerShell to upload files from compromised systems.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1025","text":"OilRig has used Wireshark’s usbcapcmd utility to capture USB traffic.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1113","text":"OilRig has a tool called CANDYKING to capture a screenshot of user's desktop.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"}]},{"id":"T1115","text":"OilRig has used infostealer tools to copy clipboard data.","cites":[{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government"}]},{"id":"T1119","text":"OilRig has used automated collection.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"}]},{"id":"T0869","text":"OilRig communicated with its command and control using HTTP requests.","cites":[{"name":"Robert Falcone, Bryan Lee May 2016","url":"https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/"}]},{"id":"T1008","text":"OilRig malware ISMAgent falls back to its DNS tunneling mechanism if it is unable to reach the C2 server over HTTP.","cites":[{"name":"OilRig ISMAgent July 2017","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/07/unit42-oilrig-uses-ismdoor-variant-possibly-linked-greenbug-threat-group/"}]},{"id":"T1071.001","text":"OilRig has used HTTP for C2.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T1071.004","text":"OilRig has used DNS for C2 including the publicly available `requestbin.net` tunneling service.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T1105","text":"OilRig had downloaded remote files onto victim infrastructure.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html"},{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1219","text":"OilRig has incorporated remote monitoring and management (RMM) tools into their operations including ngrok.","cites":[{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]},{"id":"T1572","text":"OilRig has used the Plink utility and other tools to create tunnels to C2 servers.","cites":[{"name":"Unit42 OilRig Playbook 2023","url":"https://pan-unit42.github.io/playbook_viewer/?pb=evasive-serpens"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"},{"name":"FireEye APT34 July 2019","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2019/07/hard-pass-declining-apt34-invite-to-join-their-professional-network.html"}]},{"id":"T1573.002","text":"OilRig used the PowerExchange utility and other tools to create tunnels to C2 servers.","cites":[{"name":"FireEye APT34 Webinar Dec 2017","url":"https://www.brighttalk.com/webcast/10703/296317/apt34-new-targeted-attack-in-the-middle-east"}]},{"id":"T1048.003","text":"OilRig has exfiltrated data via Microsoft Exchange and over FTP separately from its primary C2 channel over DNS.","cites":[{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig Oct 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/10/unit42-oilrig-malware-campaign-updates-toolset-and-expands-targets/"},{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html"}]}],"observables":[{"kind":"file","value":"Adobe.exe","tech":"T1036.005"},{"kind":"command","value":"netstat -an","tech":"T1049"},{"kind":"command","value":"ipconfig /all","tech":"T1016"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"systeminfo","tech":"T1082"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"net.exe","tech":"T1201"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"reg.exe","tech":"T1112"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"whoami","tech":"T1033"},{"kind":"lolbin","value":"tasklist","tech":"T1057"}],"sources":[{"name":"Check Point APT34 April 2021","url":"https://research.checkpoint.com/2021/irans-apt34-returns-with-an-updated-arsenal/","desc":"Check Point. (2021, April 8). Iran’s APT34 Returns with an Updated Arsenal. Retrieved May 5, 2021."},{"name":"ClearSky OilRig Jan 2017","url":"http://www.clearskysec.com/oilrig/","desc":"ClearSky Cybersecurity. (2017, January 5). Iranian Threat Agent OilRig Delivers Digitally Signed Malware, Impersonates University of Oxford. Retrieved May 3, 2017."},{"name":"Trend Micro Earth Simnavaz October 2024","url":"https://www.trendmicro.com/en_us/research/24/j/earth-simnavaz-cyberattacks.html","desc":"Fahmy, M. et al. (2024, October 11). Earth Simnavaz (aka APT34) Levies Advanced Cyberattacks Against Middle East. Retrieved November 27, 2024."},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig May 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/05/the-oilrig-campaign-attacks-on-saudi-arabian-organizations-deliver-helminth-backdoor/","desc":"Falcone, R. and Lee, B.. (2016, May 26). The OilRig Campaign: Attacks on Saudi Arabian Organizations Deliver Helminth Backdoor. Retrieved May 3, 2017."},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig April 2017","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2017/04/unit42-oilrig-actors-provide-glimpse-development-testing-efforts/","desc":"Falcone, R.. (2017, April 27). OilRig Actors Provide a Glimpse into Development and Testing Efforts. Retrieved May 3, 2017."},{"name":"Palo Alto OilRig Oct 2016","url":"http://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2016/10/unit42-oilrig-malware-campaign-updates-toolset-and-expands-targets/","desc":"Grunzweig, J. and Falcone, R.. (2016, October 4). OilRig Malware Campaign Updates Toolset and Expands Targets. Retrieved May 3, 2017."},{"name":"IBM ZeroCleare Wiper December 2019","url":"https://securityintelligence.com/posts/new-destructive-wiper-zerocleare-targets-energy-sector-in-the-middle-east/","desc":"Kessem, L. (2019, December 4). New Destructive Wiper ZeroCleare Targets Energy Sector in the Middle East. Retrieved September 4, 2024."},{"name":"Unit 42 QUADAGENT July 2018","url":"https://researchcenter.paloaltonetworks.com/2018/07/unit42-oilrig-targets-technology-service-provider-government-agency-quadagent/","desc":"Lee, B., Falcone, R. (2018, July 25). OilRig Targets Technology Service Provider and Government Agency with QUADAGENT. Retrieved August 9, 2018."},{"name":"Crowdstrike Helix Kitten Nov 2018","url":"https://www.crowdstrike.com/blog/meet-crowdstrikes-adversary-of-the-month-for-november-helix-kitten/","desc":"Meyers, A. (2018, November 27). Meet CrowdStrike’s Adversary of the Month for November: HELIX KITTEN. Retrieved December 18, 2018."},{"name":"Microsoft Threat Actor Naming July 2023","url":"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/microsoft-365/security/intelligence/microsoft-threat-actor-naming?view=o365-worldwide","desc":"Microsoft . (2023, July 12). How Microsoft names threat actors. Retrieved November 17, 2023."},{"name":"Proofpoint Iranian Aligned Attacks JAN 2020","url":"https://www.proofpoint.com/us/corporate-blog/post/iranian-state-sponsored-and-aligned-attacks-what-you-need-know-and-steps-protect","desc":"Proofpoint. (2020, January 10). Iranian State-Sponsored and Aligned Attacks: What You Need to Know and Steps to Protect Yourself. Retrieved January 16, 2025."},{"name":"FireEye APT34 Dec 2017","url":"https://www.fireeye.com/blog/threat-research/2017/12/targeted-attack-in-middle-east-by-apt34.html","desc":"Sardiwal, M, et al. (2017, December 7). New Targeted Attack in the Middle East by APT34, a Suspected Iranian Threat Group, Using CVE-2017-11882 Exploit. Retrieved December 20, 2017."},{"name":"Secureworks COBALT GYPSY Threat Profile","url":"https://www.secureworks.com/research/threat-profiles/cobalt-gypsy","desc":"Secureworks. (n.d.). COBALT GYPSY Threat Profile. Retrieved April 14, 2021."},{"name":"Symantec Crambus OCT 2023","url":"https://www.security.com/threat-intelligence/crambus-middle-east-government","desc":"Symantec Threat Hunter Team. (2023, October 19). Crambus: New Campaign Targets Middle Eastern Government. Retrieved November 27, 2024."}],"softwareLinks":[{"id":"S0360","n":"BONDUPDATER","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0360/"},{"id":"S0160","n":"certutil","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0160/"},{"id":"S0095","n":"ftp","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0095/"},{"id":"S0170","n":"Helminth","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0170/"},{"id":"S0100","n":"ipconfig","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0100/"},{"id":"S0189","n":"ISMInjector","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0189/"},{"id":"S0349","n":"LaZagne","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0349/"},{"id":"S1169","n":"Mango","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1169/"},{"id":"S0002","n":"Mimikatz","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0002/"},{"id":"S0039","n":"Net","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0039/"},{"id":"S0104","n":"netstat","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0104/"},{"id":"S0508","n":"ngrok","t":"tool","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S0508/"},{"id":"S1170","n":"ODAgent","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/software/S1170/"},{"id":"S1172","n":"OilBooster","t":"malware","url":"https://attack.mitre.org